lastlog, wtmp and utmp exist because login writes to them.

Every distribution ships these three files, created empty. util-linux's login
records the previous login in lastlog, appends to wtmp and updates utmp, and
without them it takes its error paths -- which is where it faulted here, with
a frame pointer holding the bytes " root" and a pointer walked past the end of
the user address space: a record it never managed to fill, used as though it
had been.

Empty is the correct initial state for all three: a zero-length lastlog reads
as "never logged in" for every uid, and wtmp and utmp are append-only logs
that start out with nothing in them.
